ories so i  hope kind of going forward into the next  two thirds of the series  that some darker elements might come to  light uh that'd be really cool but so  far neon evangelion genesis has been  fantastic i immediately bought into this  world this world that has been ravaged  by an asteroid disaster of some kind  called the second impact it's not quite  a  post-apocalyptic world at least  not in the way that people typically  imagine though it clearly has had a lot  of people die  but you know the oceans have risen  entire cities are underground or  underwater and these alien kaiju which  they call angels are attacking the  cities of humanity  and so  naturally in response as humanity always  would we create giant mecca to fight  them that can of course only be piloted  by children neon evangelion genesis is  basically pacific rim or i suppose  pacific rim is basically neon evangelion  genesis and there is some really cool  world building in the first episode uh  one of those kaiju were coming to  destroy a city and it drops into the  earth like they slot into this  underground bunker of sorts i don't  think i've ever seen something on that  scale before but it was really cool to  see  um also it did come out out in 1995 all  right and it may be one of those times  where you know sci-fi didn't quite  manage to predict what sort of  technology we would have in the future  but these giant  mecca robots that fight these kaiju uh  have to run by a chord like they've got  a power chord in the back so they can  only fight within a certain radius  and i thought that was quite funny  but let's talk about the characters  because they are fantastique i just met  asuka or asuka her name is asuka and she  is  german apparently  she immediately made an impression on me  within her first couple of minutes i  remembered her name really well  she's explosive but funny and likable  but also quite complex which is really  good she's a great foil for shinji our  other main character uh she's an  experienced pilot in these makers  likewise masato was kind of this cool  mum character and one of the things that  i really liked that they did was you can  feel the age of the characters uh you  can tell by how they talk and how they  act  masato  approaches the fight with the angels  with a kind of seriousness and gravitas  that  the kids  don't necessarily seem to have it's kind  of like you know they're they're a  little bit stuck in their own world  and  that's a really nice contrast in how  they view the stuff that is happening i  do have a criticism about the characters  but i'll get to that in my criticisms  section now you might think that these  children have a huge responsibility  defending humanity and so naturally they  would spend all of their time training  and learning but you would be wrong  because they also go to school i mean  that is an old sci-fi fantasy superhero  trope you know they have their superhero  life and their normal life and they're  trying to balance between them i don't  know where the school storyline is going  because it's not actually in the series  that much it's kind of in the background  and all of our main characters are much  more in that mecca  superhero world there's not really kind  of points attention that you might  normally see you know for example  there's a school dance coming up and  they've got that all to worry about like  shinji doesn't seem to have big school  problems i don't know i'm only nine  episodes in we will see but  if there is one trope that will get me  interested in a story it is this  conspiracies i  love stories that have you know the  secret cabal of of people in the dark  planning something in the background the  end of the episode and they pick up the  phone and they go  everything's going well and then you  don't know who it is and you don't know  who you can trust and the characters are  slowly figuring that out till they're  betrayed by someone  and as far as i can tell neon